# Simplicial Spaces, Chapter 1: Introduction

The source section introduces simplicial topological spaces, simplicial ringed
spaces, simplicial schemes, and simplicial algebraic spaces; explains their
local-to-global motivation; cites references; and assumes familiarity with
the earlier *Simplicial Methods* chapter.  It also records the convention of
writing `X` rather than `X_\bullet` for a simplicial object.  These are
expository scope and reading-guidance statements, not precise mathematical
declarations.
-/
